      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this, it looks solid and professional. i really appreciate you not making it sound like a robot wrote it.\n\ni just ran this draft through a practice scanner i found online to see how it would perform, and it gave me a pretty low score because it only hit the keywords once each. i'm worried that even if it sounds good to a human, the ATS might just filter me out before a recruiter even sees it.\n\ncan we try another version? maybe we can weave those values in a bit more frequently or more deeply throughout the paragraphs? i still want it to sound natural, but i think we need to really push those specific terms to make sure the 'Value Alignment' score is high enough to pass the threshold. can you try to bump up the density of those five keywords a bit?",
      "source": "evaluator"
